@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Where .git comes from, and how gitMode is honoured in each scope

' covers: internal/workspace/mount.go, internal/manifest/manifest.go,
'         defs/cecli/harness.manifest, defs/cursor/harness.manifest,
'         defs/opencode/harness.manifest, defs/claudecode/harness.manifest
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh, defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh,
'         defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh, defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh
'
' ── THE CONTAINER SIDE: MAKING THAT MOUNT PLAN USABLE BY git ────────────────
' The plan above decides what arrives. Two shell steps then make git able to
' read it, and BOTH run in the ENTRYPOINT SHELL rather than the Go prelude:
' `proveo-entrypoint prep` is a subprocess, so anything it exports dies with it,
' and only the shell that execs the agent can hand it environment
' (_spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-process-boundary.puml).
'
' ensure_git_safe_directory. Under a subdir scope /app is the IMAGE's own
' directory, so its owner differs from the run-as uid and git refuses everything
' with "dubious ownership". The remedy is declared through git's config-env —
' GIT_CONFIG_KEY_<n>=safe.directory / GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_<n>=<dir>, appended after
' whatever GIT_CONFIG_COUNT already holds — so nothing is written to a config
' file. It is a no-op when the worktree already resolves, and it reports
' "declared <dir> safe (worktree owner differs from the run-as uid)" only once
' the declaration actually took effect.
'
' scope_git_worktree. Only under a subdir scope (PROVEO_SCOPE_REL): the
' container's worktree root is /app but only PART of the repo is mounted there,
' so git measures the whole-repo index against a partial tree and reports every
' unmounted path as deleted. Rather than write into the host's .git, git is
' pointed at a COPY of the index — cp to ~/.cache/proveo/scoped-index, exported
' as GIT_INDEX_FILE — and the unmounted paths are marked skip-worktree there.
'
' Absent-at-STARTUP means "not mounted", never "the agent deleted it": the agent
' has not run yet. Deletions it makes later still show normally. When the
' skip-worktree pass fails the step warns ("status will list unmounted paths as
' deleted") and returns 0, because a confusing `git status` must not stop a run.

component "MountSpec.Plan()" as PLAN <<app>>

node "layout: app — every def" as APP <<host>> {
  component "**A. scope == repo root**\n/app  ← whole root\n.git rides INSIDE + ro override" as A <<app>>
  component "**B. scope UNDER repo root**\n/app/<rel> + /app/.git\nits own bind" as B <<app>>
  component "**C. not a repo**\n/app  ← input dir\nNO .git" as C <<app>>
}

component """gitMode: ro|rw""\nmanifest field" as GM <<app>>
component "nested bind over .git\nlayered on the parent mount" as OVER <<app>>

PLAN ARROW_MAIN A : RepoRoot != "" && InputDir == RepoRoot
PLAN ARROW_MAIN B : RepoRoot != "" && InputDir under RepoRoot
PLAN ARROW_MAIN C : RepoRoot == ""
GM ARROW_MAIN B : its own bind carries the flag
GM ARROW_MAIN OVER : A
OVER ARROW_MAIN A

note right of B
  **Only branch B gives "".git"" a mount of its own**, because only there is the
  container's ""/app"" assembled from pieces: the scope dir lands at
  ""/app/<rel>"", so the repo root's "".git"" must be bound separately or git
  inside the container has no repository at all.

  Here the flag rides the bind itself; elsewhere it needs an override.
end note

note bottom of A
  In A and in app, ""/app"" (or ""/app"") IS the mount, so
  "".git"" arrives as ordinary content within it and inherits that mount's
  read-only flag (""workspace.mode""), never ""gitMode"".

  A bind mount's read-only flag covers the WHOLE mount, so ""gitMode"" cannot be
  expressed by the parent bind alone. ""gitOverride"" therefore layers a second,
  nested bind over "".git"" whenever the requested state differs from the
  parent's — the more specific path wins. When they agree it emits nothing,
  because the parent already gives the right answer and an extra mount is noise.

  This is the technique ""maskEnvMounts"" already uses to pin "".env"" files to
  ""/dev/null"" inside an otherwise writable tree, so the mechanism is not new
  here — only its application to "".git"".
end note

note bottom of C
  Not a repository → no "".git"" mount, which is correct rather than a
  degradation: there is no history to expose. Agents still run, and
  ""report_git_context"" prints "Not a git repository" instead of a repo summary.
end note

note right of OVER
  **No harness sets ""gitMode: ro"" today, and a contract test keeps it that way.**
  Committing, amending and branching are normal agent work, so every harness
  mounts "".git"" read-WRITE in every scope.

  cecli briefly declared ""ro"". While ""gitMode"" was only read in branch B that
  was invisible at the repo root, so the harness kept working and the
  declaration looked harmless. Honouring it everywhere turned it into a real
  block — which is exactly what made the stale declaration worth removing rather
  than preserving.

  The mechanism stays because it is now honest: if a harness ever needs a
  read-only history, declaring it will work in every scope instead of one.
end note

note bottom of PLAN
  Sibling: ""_spec/internal/workspace/subdir-scope-mounts.puml"" details what
  ELSE branch B carries — root files, ""rootDirs"" (""_spec"", ""vendor""),
  dependency trees, and the dotenv masking that spans them.
end note

' ── The container side: two shell steps in the entrypoint SHELL ──────────────
node "Agent container — the entrypoint SHELL" as SHELL <<host>> {
  component "**declare** — ""ensure_git_safe_directory""\n""GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n=safe\.directory""" as SAFE <<app>>
  component "**scope** — ""scope_git_worktree""\nonly under ""PROVEO_SCOPE_REL""" as SCOPED <<app>>
}
database "the host's "".git""\nnever written by either step" as HOSTGIT <<error>>
database """~/\.cache/proveo/scoped-index""\na COPY — ""GIT_INDEX_FILE""" as IDX <<db>>

B ARROW_MAIN SHELL : ""/app/<rel>"" + ""/app/\.git""
SAFE ARROW_MAIN SCOPED
SCOPED ARROW_MAIN IDX : ""git update-index --skip-worktree""
SCOPED ARROW_ERROR HOSTGIT : the write this exists to avoid

note top of SHELL
  **Both run in the ENTRYPOINT SHELL, not the
  Go prelude.** ""proveo-entrypoint prep"" is a
  subprocess, so anything it exports dies with
  it — only the shell that execs the agent can
  hand it environment.
end note

note bottom of SAFE
  **Under a subdir scope ""/app"" is the IMAGE's
  own directory**, so its owner differs from the
  run-as uid and git refuses everything with
  "dubious ownership". ""safe\.directory"" is
  declared via ""GIT_CONFIG_KEY_n"" — file-free.
end note

note bottom of SCOPED
  **The worktree root is ""/app"" but only PART of
  the repo is mounted there**, so git measures a
  whole-repo index against a partial tree and
  reports every unmounted path as deleted.
end note

note right of IDX
  **The fix never writes the host's "".git"".**
  The index is COPIED to
  ""~/\.cache/proveo/scoped-index"",
  ""GIT_INDEX_FILE"" points at the copy, and the
  unmounted paths are marked skip-worktree.
end note

note left of SCOPED
  **Absent at STARTUP means "not mounted".** It
  can never mean "the agent deleted it" — the
  agent has not run yet — so deletions it makes
  later still show normally, and a failed pass
  only warns rather than stopping the run.
end note
@enduml
